Sampling profiler: PS2X_PROFILE=2 also says who called the system code a sample lands in. For a sample outside the executable (the heap, memcpy, locks, waits) the stack is unwound with the x64 unwind data while the thread is still suspended, up to the first four return addresses inside the executable, and every 15 seconds the hottest call chains per thread are printed after the usual report ([profile:callers], "leaf <- caller <- its caller ..."). PS2X_PROFILE=1 is unchanged. In Metropolismania's city this showed the game thread's heap time as operator new in the GS command queue's push, its memmove as DMA chain buffers growing, and its waits as the GS queue drain before a frame buffer clear; the run is as fast as with PS2X_PROFILE=1.

